    ],
    "word_count": 50,
    "html": "<p>Kym Rapier is an American philanthropist and founder of the Kym Rapier Foundation, supporting community organisations internationally. Her business background includes founding Silver Life Fitness, part of WellMed, and running a candle company. She and healthcare entrepreneur George Rapier established family charities supporting education, older people, children and animal welfare.</p>\r\n"
  },
  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "An old sprinkler controller brought philanthropist Kym Rapier Verette back into contact with her father’s work. George Hall had designed the system for a San Antonio family decades earlier. When Doug Piper replaced it, he arranged to give Hall’s daughter the controller, a blueprint and a brass sprinkler head bearing her father’s name.\n\nDuring the handover, Piper and her husband Glenn discovered that both had attended St. Pius X school. Hearing that it was struggling, she offered a million-dollar gift. The endowment supported better teacher salaries, while the donation also helped reduce tuition and improve facilities.",
    "confidence": {
      "score": 93,
      "band": "high",
      "reason": "Full local reporting documents each step and purpose; no religious affiliation inferred."
    },
    "source_ids": [
      "S2"
    ],
    "word_count": 96,
    "html": "<p>An old sprinkler controller brought philanthropist Kym Rapier Verette back into contact with her father’s work. George Hall had designed the system for a San Antonio family decades earlier. When Doug Piper replaced it, he arranged to give Hall’s daughter the controller, a blueprint and a brass sprinkler head bearing her father’s name.</p>\r\n<p>During the handover, Piper and her husband Glenn discovered that both had attended St. Pius X school. Hearing that it was struggling, she offered a million-dollar gift. The endowment supported better teacher salaries, while the donation also helped reduce tuition and improve facilities.</p>\r\n"
  },
